---
expect: reject
mentions: memory/parent — 자식 디렉토리는
---

# Parent without an index

The guard's second rejection path: `memory/parent` has a child directory and no
`memory.md` of its own.

`mentions` has to run past the path here. The first version of this case said
`memory/parent`, which is a prefix of `memory/parent/child/memory.md` — a guard
blaming the healthy child directory printed a superset of that string and the
case still passed. The sweep now rejects a `mentions` that is a prefix of any
path the case builds.
